{"name":"Detective Coat","hex":"#8b8685","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"detective","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A police officer tasked with collecting evidence and information in order to solve a crime; an investigator.","A person employed to find information not otherwise available to the public."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Employed in detecting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/detective"},{"term":"coat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outer garment covering the upper torso and arms.","A covering of material, such as paint."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with a coating of some material.","To cover like a coat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Detective","blocks":[{"text":"A detective is an investigator, usually a member of a law enforcement agency. They often collect information to solve crimes by talking to witnesses and informants, collecting physical evidence, or searching records in databases. This leads them to arrest criminals and enable them to be convicted in court. A detective may work for the police or privately."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Oklahoma_City_Police_Homicide_Detectives.jpeg/330px-Oklahoma_City_Police_Homicide_Detectives.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detective"},{"title":"Coat","blocks":[{"text":"A coat is an outer garment for the upper body, worn by any gender for warmth or fashion. Coats typically have long sleeves and are open down the front, and closing by means of buttons, zippers, hook-and-loop fasteners, toggles, a belt, or a combination of some of these. Other possible features include collars, shoulder straps, and hoods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/FalatJulian.PortretAntoniegoWodzickiego.1900.ws.jpg/330px-FalatJulian.PortretAntoniegoWodzickiego.1900.ws.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coat"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Leman_Street_detectives.jpg/330px-Leman_Street_detectives.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Leman_Street_detectives.jpg/330px-Leman_Street_detectives.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"H Division, of police detectives, including Frederick Abberline (left, with cane), at Leman Street police station, of the London Metropolitan Police, two years before the Jack the Ripper serial killer murders of 1888. Photograph circa 1886","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeman_Street_detectives.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg/500px-Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg/1280px-Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg/500px-Allan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Allan Pinkerton (pictured here circa 1861) was, in 1850, a detective of the Chicago Police Department and, in 1851, the founder of the Pinkerton Detective Agency.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAllan_Pinkerton-retouch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Edward_Bonney.jpg/250px-Edward_Bonney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d3/Edward_Bonney.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&